From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 15:31:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] clk: sunxi-ng: a733: Let PLL_GPU0 settle after it relocks

The manual's sequence for a factor change waits 20 us after the lock
before the PLL output is used. The relock notifier of PLL_GPU0 returns
as soon as the lock bit is set, and with CLK_SET_RATE_GATE the next
consumer may open the output right after the rate change.

Wait 20 us after the lock in the notifier.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: on two boards the GPU firmware booted after
the rate change, with the output opened by the GPU right after the
relock.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733.c b/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733.c
index 7002df3a8e23..33ccf88ad8f5 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733.c
@@ -2395,13 +2395,15 @@ static const struct sunxi_ccu_desc sun60i_a733_ccu_desc = {
 };
 
 /*
- * After a factor change the manual restarts the lock detector of the PLL
- * and waits for the lock again (4.1.4.1).
+ * After a factor change the manual restarts the lock detector of the PLL,
+ * waits for the lock again and then 20 us before the output is used
+ * (4.1.4.1).
  */
 static struct ccu_pll_nb sun60i_a733_pll_gpu0_nb = {
 	.common		= &pll_gpu0_clk.common,
 	.enable		= BIT(29),	/* LOCK_ENABLE */
 	.lock		= BIT(28),
+	.delay_us	= 20,
 };
 
 static const u32 pll_regs[] = {
